<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caupolicán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1558</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caupolicán was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> war leader, or toqui, in the early years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a> against the Spanish in Chile. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lautaro">Lautaro</a>'s death in 1557 he led the resistance, but he was captured and executed by impalement at Cañete in 1558. Alonso de Ercilla's epic La Araucana made him a heroic figure of Chilean tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caupolican.jpg" alt="Caupolicán" width="312" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Toribio Medina · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caupolic%C3%A1n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
